</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.20), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1875. Salt Lake City's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.31\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.25 to +0.36), about +4.6\u00b0F since 1875.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Salt Lake City's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.06 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 15.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (24.26 in); the driest, 1979 (8.70 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 17 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}